cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use strdcheck, please cite it as below, and cite the NIST StRD."
title: strdcheck
abstract: >-
  Numerical accuracy of the Python data stack (numpy, pandas, polars, DuckDB,
  statsmodels, scipy, PyTorch) on the NIST Statistical Reference Datasets,
  measured by the log relative error, with a pytest plugin and a published
  LRE table.
type: software
authors:
  - name: strdcheck contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/h-a-forster/strdcheck"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0.dev0
keywords:
  - numerical accuracy
  - NIST StRD
  - log relative error
  - nonlinear least squares
  - statistical software
references:
  - type: data
    authors:
      - name: National Institute of Standards and Technology
    title: "NIST Statistical Reference Datasets - SRD 140"
    doi: 10.18434/T43G6C
    url: "https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/strd/"
